  "note": "Triennial election of the Lisburn Urban Council, January 1926. Fourteen members were returned without a contest, one short of the fifteen seats; the Lisburn Standard of 8 January 1926 printed the newly elected council and noted one vacancy in the South Ward. Five candidates for five seats, returned unopposed. Returned unopposed."
